1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was was also referred to as Chēng Suì (稱遂). His estimated birth was before 2310 BCE, and he was part of an imperial family with strong ancestral connections.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and Lineage
2 CONT Jiāng Sī Suì was the son of Jiāng Měi (姜美, 帝摯14) and the brother of Jiān Sī Jī (姜斯績, 帝摯15). He had multiple wives, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Yuán (姜嫄)
2 CONT
2 CONT Qìng Dū (慶都)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cháng Xī (常羲)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jiǎn Dí (簡狄)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notable Descendants
2 CONT He fathered important historical figures such as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jiāng Hòu Jì (姜后稷) – A revered ancestor in early Chinese dynastic history.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jiāng Yáo (姜堯, 唐堯, 首任帝) – Known as Emperor Yao, a legendary ruler who greatly influenced Chinese governance and culture.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jiāng Kuāng Èr (姜匡二, 帝鷙) – Another imperial figure.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Significance
2 CONT Emperor Ku, also referred to as Jiāng Sī Suì, played an essential role in the Three Sovereigns and Five Emperors period of ancient China. He is often remembered for his contributions to early governance and dynasty-building, and h
2 CONC is descendants continued shaping Chinese civilization.
