1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''The 41st Ancestor: 振興 (Zhèn Xīng)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 1158 BC. He was the 禮部侍郎 (Lǐ Bù Shì Láng) of Shang Dynasty. He continued the editing of last twenty-eight generations and has edited more thirty-seven generations lineage. Then transferred the lineage to 孫 (Sūn), 瓊 
2 CONC (qióng).
2 CONT
2 CONT His wives were 壽 (Shòu) and 通 (Tōng). Ms. Shou had two sons named 天榮 (Tiān Róng) and 西保 (Xī Bǎo). Ms. Tong had two sons named 日養 (Rì Yǎng) and 亞春 (Yà Chūn). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 振興 (Zhèn Xīng) and his wives were killed because of 妲己 (Dá Jǐ). Because they received punishment, they were not buried in a tomb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancient lineage fourth edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT The chief editor, who was the 41st Ancestor, 振興 (Zhèn Xīng), finished the lineage from the 35th Generation to the 42nd Generation.
