1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_Xian_of_Jin
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Xian of Jin (Chinese: 晉獻公; pinyin: Jìn Xiàn Gōng), personal name Ji Guizhu, was a ruler of the Jin state, reigning for 26 years. He moved the capital from Quwo (曲沃) to Jiang (絳). He was named after the Rongdi (戎狄) leader Guiz
2 CONC hu (詭諸), whom his father and predecessor, Duke Wu, captured alive.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his reign, the Jin state became one of the most powerful and largest states due to his conquests of many small neighboring states. He is also renowned for the slaughter and exile of many ducal family members of Jin and for 
2 CONC favoring one of his concubines, Li Ji.
