1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duke Wen of Zheng (鄭文公, 踕) was a ruler of the State of Zheng during ancient China. He was born between 714 BCE and 654 BCE and passed away in 628 BCE. He was the son of Duke Li of Zheng (鄭厲公, 突) and the father of D
2 CONC uke Mu of Zheng (鄭穆公, 蘭). His wives included 陳媯, 蘇女, 燕姞, 江女, and 文芈. His children included 世子華, 公子臧, 公子瑕, 公子俞彌, and Duke Mu of Zheng.
2 CONT
2 CONT The State of Zheng was a significant regional power during the Spring and Autumn period, often involved in conflicts with neighboring states. Duke Wen's lineage was part of the House of Ji, which was connected to the Royal House o
2 CONC f Zhou.
