1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Zhaozi (昭子) was a nobleman from ancient China, estimated to have lived between 544 BCE and 430 BCE. He was the son of Duke Huai of Qin (秦懷公) and the father of Duke Ling of Qin (秦靈公). His lineage was part of the Yin
2 CONC g (嬴) surname, which later became prominent in Chinese history, particularly with the Qin Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT His family played a significant role in the development of the State of Qin, which eventually unified China under Emperor Qin Shi Huang.
