2 CONT Duke Xian of Qin (Chinese: 秦獻公; pinyin: Qín Xiàn Gōng, 424–362 BC), personal name Ying Shixi or Ying Lian, was a duke of the Qin state. He reigned from 384 to 362 BC.[1][2]
